  "audience": {
    "schemaVersion": "1.0",
    "programmeDescription": "Liberal Arts and Sciences at Tilburg combines an interdisciplinary core with one of four majors and one of three societal themes. The selected pathway studies people, communities, organisations, inequality and digital life through Interdisciplinary Social Sciences, alongside Transformations to Sustainability. It leads to a Bachelor of Science.",
    "comparisonExplanation": "UCR approaches these interests through society, organisations and sustainable public challenges; cognition and behaviour; or law, politics and contested culture. Each combines substantive disciplinary inquiry with research and broader perspectives. The comparison follows one defined Tilburg pathway, while the two related UCR directions also draw on its other established majors. Shared rows show partial subject relationships. Tilburg’s integrated core subjects, Senior Seminar, theme capstone and required thesis remain meaningful differences.",
